# Autoloop run logs. Keep the per-run chatter ignored, but TRACK the append-only
# run trace so an accidental overwrite is recoverable (GH #88: wake 84 replaced
# it and lost ~107 KB / wakes 1-83 with no git copy). `logs/*` rather than `logs/`
# so the negation below can descend into the directory.
logs/*
*.log
!logs/STATE.log
# GH #83: the single-instance lock is runtime state, not source. It is removed by
# the runner's `finally`, but a killed runner can leave one behind for takeover.
loop.lock.json
loop.lock.json.tmp
